## Branch update base

The publication base is `main`. Branch updates target `origin/main`; follow the update method in the selected checklist. Follow-up runs use their contribution family's base; after retargeting they use the recorded retarget branch. Keep default-branch freshness checks separate.
For a rebase, first fetch the PR head and record its exact remote SHA in `artifacts/pre-rebase-remote-sha.txt` under this task. Refuse an update if local HEAD omits remote commits. After conflict resolution and the required checks, push the rebased branch with an explicit lease against that recorded SHA. Never infer the update base from a PR body or replace it with the default branch while the upstream PR remains open.

Run this shared operation before any rebase or up-to-date shortcut. It performs the verified rebase; do not run an additional rebase:

```bash
node '<FARMSLOT_ROOT>/packages/agent-runtime/scripts/branch-update.mjs' execute '{"kind":"ordinary","repo":"<FARMSLOT_ROOT>","branch":"feature/golden-pr","baseRef":"main"}'
```

After conflict resolution, required checks and any fix commits, use this shared leased push:

```bash
node '<FARMSLOT_ROOT>/packages/agent-runtime/scripts/branch-update.mjs' push '{"kind":"ordinary","repo":"<FARMSLOT_ROOT>","branch":"feature/golden-pr","baseRef":"main"}'
```

## Recipe proof + acceptance review

Prefix every task proof invocation with `RECIPE_TASK_DIR="$(cd ".sandbox/farmslot-farm/worker-task/fix/<TASK_ID>" && pwd)"` in the same shell call as the configured recipe command. A separate export does not survive a later shell call. Direct host invocations must use a fresh directory under `.sandbox/farmslot-farm/worker-task/fix/<TASK_ID>/artifacts/recipe-runs/`; fixed or diagnostic output directories do not select task proof. Independent diagnostics must omit task binding.
Inspect registered criteria with `node "<FARMSLOT_ROOT>/packages/agent-runtime/bin/farmslot-agent.mjs" ac list --task-dir ".sandbox/farmslot-farm/worker-task/fix/<TASK_ID>"`. Declare their IDs and claims in the recipe's `proofTargets` and bind qualifying assertion nodes through `proves`. Run the recipe through the configured command and inspect its retained results. Recipe execution produces normal verdicts; never set a proven verdict by hand or edit acceptance ledger rows. Retain unresolved results. When the captured completion contract permits human review, present them at the run gate and ask an authorized person for an untestable override with a reason. Without that gate, completion still refuses.
Inspect the criteria again. When recipe.json exists, render coverage with `node "<FARMSLOT_ROOT>/packages/agent-runtime/bin/farmslot-agent.mjs" ac render --task-dir ".sandbox/farmslot-farm/worker-task/fix/<TASK_ID>"` to a temporary file, then replace `artifacts/recipe-coverage.md` only after a successful render. Run `node "<FARMSLOT_ROOT>/packages/agent-runtime/bin/farmslot-agent.mjs" artifact-check ".sandbox/farmslot-farm/worker-task/fix/<TASK_ID>" --contract ".sandbox/farmslot-farm/worker-task/fix/<TASK_ID>/inputs/worker-terminal-contract.json" --terminal complete --require-recipe-coverage-if-recipe --require-acceptance-status` before `mark complete`. Missing ledgers, unrecorded criterion rows and integrity failures refuse completion. Valid selected unresolved verdicts can reach the configured human gate; they do not grant approval. Checked checklist items alone do not assess an AC.

